  "description": "NEZSOE crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C32 H80 Cl6 Co2 O21 Pr4,0.5(C3 H8 O2),0.25(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.309-5.265 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.64-179.85°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C30H72Cl6Co2O21Pr4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
